Think: Good! The timestamps were extracted successfully. Now I need to normalize entries in "timestamps.txt" to strict two-digit hour and minute format, remove any malformed lines, and write the clean results to "normalized_timestamps.txt" while recording the number of removed lines to "errors.log". I need to ensure all hours are in HH format (two digits).

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
    if (match($0, /^[0-9]{1,2}:[0-9]{2}$/)) {
        split($0, parts, ":");
        hour = parts[1];
        minute = parts[2];
        if (length(hour) == 1) hour = "0" hour;
        if (hour >= 0 && hour <= 23 && minute >= 0 && minute <= 59) {
            print hour ":" minute;
        } else {
            print $0 > "temp_workspace/errors.log";
            error_count++;
        }
    } else {
        print $0 > "temp_workspace/errors.log";
        error_count++;
    }
} END {
    if (error_count > 0) {
        print "Removed " error_count " malformed lines" > "temp_workspace/errors.log";
    } else {
        print "0 malformed lines removed" > "temp_workspace/errors.log";
    }
}' temp_workspace/timestamps.txt > temp_workspace/normalized_timestamps.txt
```

